{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1732, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nThere are N snakes.\nInitially, the thickness of the i-th snake is T_i, and its length is L_i.\nThe weight of a snake is defined as the product of its thickness and length.\nFor each integer k satisfying 1 \\leq k \\leq D, find the weight of the heaviest snake when every snake's length has increased by k.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN D\r\nT_1 L_1\r\nT_2 L_2\r\n\\vdots\r\nT_N L_N\n\nOutput\n\nPrint D lines. The k-th line should contain the weight of the heaviest snake when every snake's length has increased by k.\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- 1 \\leq N, D \\leq 100\n- 1 \\leq T_i, L_i \\leq 100\n- All input values are integers.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n4 3\r\n3 3\r\n5 1\r\n2 4\r\n1 10\n\nSample Output 1\n\n12\r\n15\r\n20\r\n\nWhen every snake\u2019s length has increased by 1, the snakes' weights become 12, 10, 10, 11, so print 12 on the first line.\nWhen every snake\u2019s length has increased by 2, the snakes' weights become 15, 15, 12, 12, so print 15 on the second line.\nWhen every snake\u2019s length has increased by 3, the snakes' weights become 18, 20, 14, 13, so print 20 on the third line.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n1 4\r\n100 100\n\nSample Output 2\n\n10100\r\n10200\r\n10300\r\n10400\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1788, "char_start": 1744, "quote": "Input:\n4 3\n3 3\n5 1\n2 4\n1 10\nOutput:\n12\n15\n20", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1850, "char_start": 1800, "quote": "Input:\n1 4\n100 100\nOutput:\n10100\n10200\n10300\n10400", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "9f6f3a5cb7ce91e61640129e31f24ccd8bc50f60729fa49d453009061c17769a", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "84568a179c99f898f61e44764705c4f5e5f6fd364aed93dfd75b27e68055a429", "seq": 2}
